  ('IO-CM-MP-0001', 'Project-affected communities resume protest over rehabilitation and compensation in Bundelkhand', 'Multi-form civic protest', 'Rehabilitation, compensation and displacement linked to the Ken–Betwa Link Project and other development projects', 'Madhya Pradesh', 'Chhatarpur / Panna', 'Near Kupi village in the Chhatarpur–Panna project-affected area', '2026-07-04', null, 'ongoing', 'Project-affected tribal and farming communities resumed a protest in early July 2026 in the Chhatarpur–Panna area of Madhya Pradesh. Reported forms of protest include a symbolic Chita Andolan, Jal Satyagraha, hunger strike and Mitti Satyagraha. Participants have publicly raised concerns about compensation, rehabilitation and displacement. The occurrence and principal demands are corroborated; allegations about water access, compensation irregularities and the full implementation of relief measures remain attributed or under review.', 'occurrence_verified_disputed_details', '2026-07-15', '2026-07-15', 'candidate', 'in_national_pilot', '2026-07-15', 'The X post was published on 15 July 2026; the exact filming date is not independently confirmed. Sources describe Kupi''s district inconsistently, so the public wording uses the broader Chhatarpur–Panna project-affected area.', 'multiple_phases', 'Land & rehabilitation', 'Compensation / land rights', 'Ken–Betwa Link Project', '2026-07-10', '2026-07-22', 'User-provided lead', 'Social-first, later corroborated', 'District administration stated that demands had been addressed; protesters disputed that assessment.'),
  ('IO-CM-DL-0001', 'Education accountability sit-in and hunger strike continues at Jantar Mantar', 'Multi-form civic protest', 'Alleged examination irregularities, paper leaks and demand for education-system accountability', 'Delhi', 'New Delhi', 'Jantar Mantar, New Delhi', '2026-06-20', null, 'ongoing', 'A sit-in organised by the Cockroach Janta Party continued at Jantar Mantar in New Delhi in July 2026, with participants demanding accountability over alleged examination irregularities and the resignation of Union Education Minister Dharmendra Pradhan. Education reformer Sonam Wangchuk joined the action through an indefinite hunger strike from 28 June. The occurrence, location and principal demand are independently corroborated; reported medical details and some examination-related claims remain attributed to organisers or media reports.', 'occurrence_verified_disputed_details', '2026-07-15', '2026-07-15', 'candidate', 'in_national_pilot', '2026-07-15', 'The protest began before the 1 July research window but remained active during it. Medical information is not treated as independently verified unless supported by identifiable clinical documentation. A proposed 20 July march is recorded only as an announcement, not as an event that has occurred.', 'continuous', 'Education', 'Accountability / resignation', 'Examination integrity and Union Ministry of Education accountability', '2026-07-14', '2026-07-20', 'National media search', 'Nationally covered', 'The Union education minister rejected calls to resign; organisers announced further action.'),
  ('IO-CM-KA-0001', 'Mandya farmers intensify protest demanding release of KRS irrigation water', 'Demonstration', 'Immediate release of canal water from the KRS reservoir for standing crops', 'Karnataka', 'Mandya', 'Deputy Commissioner’s office and Sanjay Circle, Mandya', '2026-07-13', null, 'ongoing', 'Farmers and supporting organisations protested in Mandya on 13 July 2026, demanding the immediate release of water from the Krishnaraja Sagar reservoir into irrigation canals. Independent reports documented a demonstration near the deputy commissioner’s office and a blockade of the old Mysuru–Bengaluru highway. Protesters said standing crops were drying because of the delay and opposed additional diversion of Cauvery water while irrigation needs remained unmet. The occurrence and stated demands are corroborated; crop-loss severity remains attributed to protesters.', 'occurrence_verified_disputed_details', '2026-07-15', '2026-07-15', 'candidate', 'in_national_pilot', '2026-07-14', 'Reports describe the action as part of an intensifying agitation. The record does not independently calculate crop losses or determine legal water-allocation obligations.', 'recurring_intermittent', 'Agriculture & water', 'Resource allocation', 'KRS irrigation-water release and Cauvery water management', '2026-07-15', '2026-07-18', 'Regional / local media', 'Regional coverage', 'Reporting said the state was awaiting the water-management authority''s position while farmers continued to demand release.'),
  ('IO-CM-CH-0001', 'BKU-Rajewal holds Chandigarh motorcycle rally over proposed India–US trade agreement', 'March', 'Opposition to the proposed India–US trade agreement and concerns affecting Punjab agriculture', 'Chandigarh', 'Chandigarh', 'Route from Phase 8, Mohali, to the Exhibition Ground in Sector 34, Chandigarh', '2026-07-13', '2026-07-13', 'concluded', 'The Bharatiya Kisan Union (Rajewal) held a motorcycle and vehicle rally from Mohali to Chandigarh on 13 July 2026. Participants called for rejection of the proposed India–US trade agreement, arguing that greater agricultural imports could disadvantage small farmers and allied sectors. Organisers also raised Punjab-specific concerns including groundwater quality, land acquisition and natural resources. Independent reports documented the route, traffic restrictions and submission of memorandums; predictions about the trade agreement’s effects remain attributed to organisers.', 'occurrence_verified_disputed_details', '2026-07-15', '2026-07-15', 'candidate', 'in_national_pilot', '2026-07-13', 'This record covers the 13 July BKU-Rajewal rally, not the separate farmer rally held in Chandigarh on 10 July. Future protest announcements are not treated as completed events.', 'one_day', 'Trade & economic policy', 'Policy withdrawal / amendment', 'Proposed India–US trade agreement', '2026-07-13', '2026-07-27', 'Regional / local media', 'Regional coverage', 'Police imposed traffic controls and organisers submitted memorandums to Union and state authorities.'),
  ('IO-CM-MH-0001', 'Citizens form human chain in Thane under the Save SGNP campaign', 'Civic campaign', 'Protection of forests and eco-sensitive areas surrounding Sanjay Gandhi National Park', 'Maharashtra', 'Thane', 'Chitalsar Manpada entry area and the Tikuji-ni-Wadi–Khewra Chowk stretch, Thane', '2026-07-05', '2026-07-05', 'concluded', 'Residents, trekkers, environmentalists and other supporters gathered in Thane on 5 July 2026 as part of the Save SGNP campaign. Reports documented a protest and human chain opposing infrastructure and construction proposals near Sanjay Gandhi National Park and surrounding forest areas. One stated demand was to stop a proposed man-made biodiversity park in an area protesters described as already ecologically sensitive. The occurrence is corroborated; campaign claims about exact attendance and the precise area at risk remain attributed pending official land and project records.', 'occurrence_verified_disputed_details', '2026-07-15', '2026-07-15', 'candidate', 'in_national_pilot', '2026-07-05', 'The Times of India identifies the Sunday protest as 5 July 2026. A Free Press Journal report refers to Sunday, 6 July, but 6 July 2026 was Monday; the event date is therefore recorded as 5 July with the discrepancy logged.', 'one_day', 'Environment', 'Environmental protection', 'Sanjay Gandhi National Park and proposed nearby development projects', null, '2026-08-05', 'Petition / campaign page', 'Community-source led', 'No direct authority response had been added; follow-up is required on project documents and land status.'),
  ('IO-CM-KA-0002', 'Bidadi farmers continue protest against land acquisition for Greater Bengaluru Integrated Township', 'Multi-form civic protest', 'Land acquisition, agricultural livelihoods, compensation, consent and environmental concerns linked to the Greater Bengaluru Integrated Township', 'Karnataka', 'Bengaluru South (formerly Ramanagara)', 'Bidadi region, including Byramangala, Kanchugaranahalli, Kempayyanapalya, Mandalahalli and Vaderahalli', null, null, 'ongoing', 'Farmers and agricultural communities around Bidadi have conducted a sustained movement opposing land acquisition for the proposed Greater Bengaluru Integrated Township. The movement includes village meetings, marches, an Appiko tree-hugging action and resistance to land-survey activity. Protesters say the project threatens agricultural livelihoods and has proceeded without adequate consent or consultation. The Karnataka government describes the township as a planned urban-development and employment project and has offered compensation options. The protest''s occurrence and the first-phase acquisition notification are corroborated; claims concerning consent levels, the fertility and extent of affected farmland, environmental loss and responsibility for violence during survey operations remain attributed or disputed.', 'occurrence_verified_disputed_details', '2026-07-15', '2026-07-15', 'candidate', 'in_national_pilot', '2026-07-15', 'Exact movement start date remains under verification. Independent reporting states that farmers had protested for more than 450 days by 29 June 2026. The record must not present the actions of individuals during the 13 July survey confrontation as actions of the entire movement. The reported government review committee is included as an attributed official response pending a direct government order or committee notification.', 'recurring_intermittent', 'Land & rehabilitation', 'Project cancellation / withdrawal', 'Greater Bengaluru Integrated Township', '2026-07-15', '2026-07-22', 'User-provided lead', 'Social-first, later corroborated', 'Media reported that the Karnataka government announced a review committee; the formal notification remains to be obtained.'),
  ('IO-CM-GJ-0001', 'Morbi farmers continue satyagraha over compensation for power-transmission infrastructure', 'Multi-form civic protest', 'Compensation and agricultural-land impacts linked to high-voltage transmission towers and right-of-way corridors', 'Gujarat', 'Morbi and other affected districts', 'Jetpar village, Morbi district, with affected farmers across multiple Gujarat districts', '2026-06-07', null, 'ongoing', 'Farmers centred in Jetpar village, Morbi, conducted a multi-phase movement against the compensation terms for agricultural land affected by a high-voltage power-transmission project. The movement included demonstrations, symbolic head-shaving and an indefinite hunger strike that began on 17 June. After the Gujarat government issued revised compensation guidelines on 4 July, the farmers ended the fast but said the agitation would continue as a satyagraha because questions remained about land valuation, right-of-way compensation and implementation. The movement and government response are independently corroborated; claims about land becoming uncultivable and the exact number of affected farmers remain attributed.', 'occurrence_verified_disputed_details', '2026-07-15', '2026-07-15', 'candidate', 'in_national_pilot', '2026-07-07', 'The Indian Express reported a 756 kV double-circuit line and a 246 km route, while other reporting described 765 kV infrastructure and a 301 km first-phase route. These technical figures are not used in the public summary until official project documents are added.', 'multiple_phases', 'Land & rehabilitation', 'Compensation / land rights', 'Halvad Transmission / Adani Energy Solutions transmission project and Gujarat compensation resolution', '2026-07-04', '2026-07-22', 'Community social media', 'Social-first, later corroborated', 'The Gujarat government issued revised compensation guidelines; farmers ended the hunger strike on 7 July but continued the agitation as a satyagraha.'),
  ('IO-CM-UP-0001', 'Dasiya villagers protest construction of an ethanol plant in Basti district', 'Demonstration', 'Environmental, water, health and land-consent concerns relating to a proposed ethanol plant', 'Uttar Pradesh', 'Basti', 'Dasiya village, Rudhauli police-station area, Bhanpur tehsil', '2026-06-23', null, 'ongoing', 'Residents of Dasiya and nearby villages have opposed an ethanol plant under construction in Basti district. A memorandum submitted in June raised concerns about nearby settlements and government schools, while a larger demonstration was announced and held on 14 July under substantial police deployment. Protesters called for the factory to be stopped and raised concerns about water use, environmental and health effects, and the circumstances in which land was obtained. The occurrence and continuing opposition are corroborated through local-language reporting and public field material; allegations that residents were misled about the project and specific impact estimates remain attributed.', 'occurrence_verified_disputed_details', '2026-07-15', '2026-07-15', 'candidate', 'in_national_pilot', '2026-07-14', 'The company name and full environmental-clearance record have not yet been confirmed. Claims that land was obtained by describing a different type of factory are allegations and require deeds, consent records or official inquiry documents.', 'recurring_intermittent', 'Environment', 'Project cancellation / withdrawal', 'Dasiya ethanol plant and India''s ethanol-blending programme', '2026-07-14', '2026-07-21', 'Community social media', 'Social-first, later corroborated', 'Police and district officials deployed heavily and stopped some political representatives from reaching the factory area; no substantive project decision has yet been located.'),
  ('IO-CM-AS-0001', 'Bodo residents protest proposed APDCL land allotment and resettlement plan in Kokrajhar', 'Demonstration', 'Protection of Tribal Belt and Block land from proposed allotment and resettlement', 'Assam', 'Kokrajhar', 'Malgaon area near the Kokrajhar district border', '2026-07-12', '2026-07-12', 'concluded', 'Hundreds of Bodo residents gathered at Malgaon on 12 July 2026 to oppose a proposed land allotment to Assam Power Distribution Company Limited and the proposed rehabilitation of 93 families evicted from Kaimari. Protesters demanded protection of land they described as part of a Tribal Belt and Block and called for the allotment and resettlement proposal to be withdrawn. The demonstration is supported by regional video reporting and local community coverage. The legal status and exact acreage of the land, the government''s decision-making record and the rights of all affected communities require official documents and careful follow-up.', 'occurrence_verified_disputed_details', '2026-07-15', '2026-07-15', 'candidate', 'in_national_pilot', '2026-07-12', 'This record must not stigmatise or assign wrongdoing to the 93 families proposed for rehabilitation. The public-interest question is the land-allotment and consultation process, not the identity of displaced families.', 'one_day', 'Land & rehabilitation', 'Legal protection / rights', 'Proposed APDCL land allotment, Tribal Belt and Block protections, and rehabilitation proposal', null, '2026-07-19', 'Community social media', 'Undercovered / remote', 'No direct government or BTC response had been located at the time of review; protesters warned that democratic agitation would continue.'),
  ('IO-CM-MN-0001', 'Manipur government employees continue indefinite cease-work strike over pay and service conditions', 'Strike', 'Dearness allowance, pension, retirement age, contractual employment and weekly-holiday demands', 'Manipur', 'Statewide', 'Government offices across Manipur, including Imphal and district headquarters', '2026-07-01', null, 'ongoing', 'The Manipur Government Services Federation launched an indefinite cease-work strike on 1 July 2026 over a multi-point charter concerning dearness allowance, pension arrangements, retirement age, contractual appointments and weekly holidays. Reporting from regional and state-level outlets documented significant disruption to routine administrative work. The government restored Saturday as a holiday and introduced a five-day work week, but the federation said the strike would continue because other demands remained unresolved. The occurrence, duration and partial government response are corroborated; estimates of financial loss and the precise participation level remain attributed.', 'occurrence_verified_disputed_details', '2026-07-15', '2026-07-15', 'candidate', 'in_national_pilot', '2026-07-15', 'Do not merge this MGSF-led strike with separate July cease-work actions organised by the JAC of AMTUC and AMGEO unless organisational coordination is independently confirmed.', 'continuous', 'Labour & employment', 'Pay / pension / service conditions', 'Manipur government service rules, DA/DR parity, pension policy and five-day work-week notification', '2026-07-10', '2026-07-20', 'Regional / local media', 'Regional coverage', 'The government restored Saturday as a holiday and introduced a five-day working week, but MGSF said the strike would continue over remaining demands.'),
  ('IO-CM-OD-0001', 'Dharmasala high-school students stage dharna over teacher vacancies', 'Sit-in / Dharna', 'Teacher shortages affecting a rural government school''s academic functioning', 'Odisha', 'Jajpur', 'Dharmasala Baneepeetha High School, Dharmasala block', '2026-07-10', '2026-07-10', 'concluded', 'Students of Dharmasala Baneepeetha High School in Jajpur district locked the school gate and staged a dharna on 10 July 2026, demanding immediate appointment of teachers. Independent local reports agreed that several posts were vacant and that students said the shortage was affecting their studies, although the reports differed on the precise number of teachers and students. District education officials responded the same day by deputing two teachers, after which the students withdrew the protest. The event, demand and immediate response are corroborated; remaining staffing vacancies require follow-up.', 'occurrence_verified_disputed_details', '2026-07-15', '2026-07-15', 'candidate', 'in_national_pilot', '2026-07-10', 'The New Indian Express reported 11 teachers and more than 400 students in Classes VIII–X; The Times of India reported 10 teachers and 508 students in Classes I–X. The discrepancy may reflect different counted sections or timing and must remain visible.', 'one_day', 'Education', 'Service delivery / staffing', 'Sanctioned teacher strength and staffing of Dharmasala Baneepeetha High School', '2026-07-10', '2026-07-24', 'Field video / citizen post', 'Local media only', 'District education officials deputed two teachers on the day of the protest; students then withdrew the dharna.'),
  ('IO-CM-UK-0001', 'Residents continue protest against tree felling for Bhaniyawala–Rishikesh highway widening', 'Multi-form civic protest', 'Tree felling, forest and wildlife-corridor impacts linked to the Bhaniyawala–Jollygrant–Rishikesh road-widening project', 'Uttarakhand', 'Dehradun', 'Bhaniyawala–Rishikesh stretch, including Saat Mod and the Shivalik reserve, Dehradun district', '2026-07-08', null, 'ongoing', 'Residents and environmental activists in Dehradun district organised protests against tree felling for the Bhaniyawala–Jollygrant–Rishikesh highway-widening project. Documented actions included a demonstration at the NHAI office, tree-hugging and sit-ins along the road stretch. Tree felling later resumed under police deployment, and media reported arrests and an FIR against unidentified protesters. The occurrence and protest methods are corroborated; the precise number of trees affected and some project-impact claims remain disputed or dependent on official records.', 'occurrence_verified_disputed_details', '2026-07-17', '2026-07-17', 'candidate', 'in_national_pilot', '2026-07-15', 'The earliest directly reviewed protest report is dated 8 July 2026; a later report described 11 July as the fifth consecutive day, suggesting activity may have begun around 7 July. Two user-provided X posts are retained only as social-media leads. The Mohammad Aman post shows a roadside environmental appeal with felled trees, but exact location, capture date and original creator remain unconfirmed; the Swati Negi post has not yet been fully captured. Treat the two posts as a possible shared source family until provenance is resolved. Published figures for trees affected differ across sources.', 'multiple_phases', 'Environment', 'Environmental protection', 'Bhaniyawala–Jollygrant–Rishikesh Four/Six Laning Project (NH-07), forest and wildlife clearances', '2026-07-07', '2026-07-24', 'User-provided lead', 'Social-first, later corroborated', 'NHAI said the project uses a reduced right of way, tree transplantation and wildlife-mitigation measures; protesters continued to seek a halt or deferment of tree felling.'),
  ('IO-CM-HR-0001', 'Haryana farmers protest biometric and other new Rabi procurement requirements', 'Multi-form civic protest', 'Biometric verification, portal rules and access to government wheat and mustard procurement', 'Haryana', 'Multiple districts including Jind', 'Grain markets, toll plazas and roads across Haryana', '2026-04-05', '2026-04-20', 'outcome_pending', 'Farmer organisations in Haryana staged coordinated protests in April 2026 against biometric verification and other new Rabi procurement procedures. Actions included market sit-ins, road blockades and an indefinite protest in Jind. The state defended the system as a transparency and anti-irregularity measure. The occurrence and policy dispute are corroborated; the final resolution was not located in the reviewed sources.', 'occurrence_verified_disputed_details', '2026-07-17', '2026-07-17', 'candidate', 'in_national_pilot', '2026-04-20', 'The earliest reviewed protest report is dated 5 April. Protests continued through at least 20 April. Claims about exclusion from procurement, portal failures and farmer losses require transaction-level procurement records.', 'multiple_phases', 'Agriculture & water', 'Service delivery / procurement', 'Haryana Rabi procurement and biometric verification system', '2026-04-04', '2026-05-05', 'Regional / local media', 'Regional coverage', 'The Haryana government defended the biometric and portal-based procurement system as a transparency measure and continued procurement operations.'),
  ('IO-CM-HR-0002', 'Manesar industrial workers protest wages and working conditions', 'Multi-form civic protest', 'Minimum wages, rising living costs and industrial working conditions', 'Haryana', 'Gurugram', 'IMT Manesar industrial area', '2026-04-07', '2026-04-10', 'concluded', 'Industrial workers in Manesar protested in April 2026 for higher wages and improved working conditions amid rising living costs. Work stoppages and street demonstrations affected several units, and clashes were reported on 9 April. Haryana then announced a substantial minimum-wage revision. The protest and wage response are corroborated; responsibility for violence remains attributed.', 'occurrence_verified_disputed_details', '2026-07-17', '2026-07-17', 'candidate', 'in_national_pilot', '2026-04-10', 'Police allegations concerning conspiracy, arson or responsibility for violence are not treated as established findings. Participation and production-impact estimates differ across sources.', 'multiple_phases', 'Labour & employment', 'Pay / wages', 'Haryana minimum-wage notification and industrial labour regulation', '2026-04-10', '2026-05-10', 'National media search', 'Nationally covered', 'Haryana announced a 35% minimum-wage increase effective from 1 April 2026 and urged workers to resume duties peacefully.'),
  ('IO-CM-UP-0002', 'Noida factory workers protest wages, hours and overtime conditions', 'Multi-form civic protest', 'Wage increases, fixed working hours, overtime payments and factory labour conditions', 'Uttar Pradesh', 'Gautam Buddha Nagar', 'Industrial areas of Noida', '2026-04-08', '2026-04-14', 'concluded', 'Factory workers in Noida protested in April 2026 seeking higher wages, regulated working hours and improved overtime payments. The protests escalated into clashes on 13 April, and police used tear gas. Uttar Pradesh subsequently announced a minimum-wage increase. The occurrence and policy response are corroborated; responsibility for violence remains disputed.', 'occurrence_verified_disputed_details', '2026-07-17', '2026-07-17', 'candidate', 'in_national_pilot', '2026-04-14', 'Do not attribute stone-pelting, arson or other acts to the full worker movement. Arrest numbers, participation and responsibility for damage are police or media accounts pending case records.', 'multiple_phases', 'Labour & employment', 'Pay / wages', 'Uttar Pradesh minimum-wage and factory labour regulation', '2026-04-14', '2026-05-14', 'National media search', 'Nationally covered', 'Uttar Pradesh raised minimum wages and announced labour-administration measures after the protests.'),
  ('IO-CM-DL-0002', 'Jamia students protest an RSS-linked Yuva Kumbh event on campus', 'Demonstration', 'Campus autonomy, ideological events and allegations concerning treatment of protesting students', 'Delhi', 'New Delhi', 'Jamia Millia Islamia campus', '2026-04-28', '2026-04-28', 'concluded', 'Students at Jamia Millia Islamia protested on 28 April 2026 against an RSS-linked Yuva Kumbh programme on campus. Police and CRPF personnel were deployed, and students and the university issued conflicting accounts about the removal of protesters and alleged injuries. The protest and deployment are corroborated; injury totals and force allegations remain disputed.', 'occurrence_verified_disputed_details', '2026-07-17', '2026-07-17', 'candidate', 'in_national_pilot', '2026-04-28', 'Student groups and university officials gave conflicting accounts about crowd size, manhandling and injuries. No medical or independent injury record was reviewed.', 'one_day', 'Education', 'Institutional policy / campus governance', 'Jamia campus event permissions and student-protest rules', '2026-04-28', '2026-05-15', 'National media search', 'Nationally covered', 'The university allowed the programme to proceed and disputed allegations of manhandling.'),
  ('IO-CM-KL-0001', 'Kerala hotels, restaurants and bakeries shut over commercial LPG prices', 'Strike', 'Commercial LPG price increases and operating costs for hospitality businesses', 'Kerala', 'Statewide', 'Hospitality businesses across Kerala; demonstrations at petroleum-company offices', '2026-05-06', '2026-05-06', 'concluded', 'Hotels, restaurants, bakeries and allied hospitality businesses across Kerala observed a 24-hour shutdown on 6 May 2026 over a sharp increase in commercial LPG prices. Organisers also held marches and dharnas at petroleum-company and central-government offices. The shutdown and public impact are independently documented.', 'occurrence_verified_disputed_details', '2026-07-17', '2026-07-17', 'candidate', 'in_national_pilot', '2026-05-06', 'Organiser estimates concerning the proportion of establishments closed, commercial losses and future job losses were not independently audited.', 'one_day', 'Trade & economic policy', 'Price / tax relief', 'Commercial LPG pricing', null, '2026-05-15', 'Regional / local media', 'Regional coverage', 'No immediate rollback of the commercial LPG increase was located in the reviewed sources.'),
  ('IO-CM-PB-0001', 'Punjab Roadways, PUNBUS and PRTC contract workers hold gate rallies', 'Demonstration', 'Regularisation, release of jailed colleagues and opposition to transport privatisation', 'Punjab', 'Statewide', 'Punjab Roadways, PUNBUS and PRTC depots', '2026-05-15', '2026-05-15', 'concluded', 'Contract workers of Punjab Roadways, PUNBUS and PRTC held gate rallies at depots across Punjab on 15 May 2026. Their demands included release of jailed colleagues, regularisation and opposition to the kilometre scheme. The rallies are corroborated; legal and employment-status claims remain attributed.', 'occurrence_verified_disputed_details', '2026-07-17', '2026-07-17', 'candidate', 'in_national_pilot', '2026-05-15', 'The legal status of jailed colleagues, the number of affected contract workers and claims about privatisation require police, court and employment records.', 'one_day', 'Labour & employment', 'Regularisation / employment security', 'Punjab public transport contracting, Special Cadre Policy and kilometre scheme', null, '2026-06-11', 'Union / civil-society channel', 'Regional coverage', 'A later written agreement addressed some demands and led to cancellation of a subsequent strike.'),
  ('IO-CM-DL-0003', 'Student organisations protest the alleged NEET-UG paper leak in Delhi', 'Multi-form civic protest', 'Alleged NEET-UG paper leak, examination cancellation and accountability of the testing system', 'Delhi', 'New Delhi', 'National Testing Agency office, Education Minister''s residence and Jantar Mantar', '2026-05-13', '2026-05-15', 'outcome_pending', 'Student organisations protested in Delhi from 13 to 15 May 2026 over the cancellation of NEET-UG following allegations of a paper leak. Demonstrations occurred outside the National Testing Agency, the Education Minister''s residence and at Jantar Mantar. The protests are corroborated; criminal responsibility and the scale of the leak remain subject to investigation.', 'occurrence_verified_disputed_details', '2026-07-17', '2026-07-17', 'candidate', 'in_national_pilot', '2026-05-15', 'Claims about who caused the leak, the number of affected candidates and political responsibility are not treated as established beyond official investigation and court findings.', 'multiple_phases', 'Education', 'Accountability / investigation', 'NEET-UG examination administration and investigation', '2026-05-12', '2026-06-15', 'National media search', 'Nationally covered', 'Investigation and re-examination measures were announced, while student groups continued to demand accountability.'),
  ('IO-CM-TS-0001', 'Student groups protest the alleged NEET-UG paper leak in Hyderabad', 'Demonstration', 'Examination integrity, alleged NEET-UG paper leak and accountability of education authorities', 'Telangana', 'Hyderabad', 'Lok Bhavan, RTC Crossroads and other protest sites in Hyderabad', '2026-05-13', '2026-05-14', 'concluded', 'Student organisations in Hyderabad staged protests on 13 and 14 May 2026 over the alleged NEET-UG paper leak and cancellation. Separate groups demonstrated at Lok Bhavan, RTC Crossroads and other sites. The occurrence and demands are independently documented; responsibility for the leak remains under investigation.', 'occurrence_verified_disputed_details', '2026-07-17', '2026-07-17', 'candidate', 'in_national_pilot', '2026-05-14', 'Statements about the number of affected students, official culpability and repeated leaks are advocacy claims unless tied to verified examination and investigative records.', 'multiple_phases', 'Education', 'Accountability / investigation', 'NEET-UG examination administration', null, '2026-06-15', 'Regional / local media', 'Regional coverage', 'Police controlled access to official sites and detained some protesters; no direct settlement was located.'),
  ('IO-CM-RJ-0001', 'Congress workers protest alleged NEET irregularities in Jaipur', 'March', 'Alleged NEET-UG irregularities and accountability of education authorities', 'Rajasthan', 'Jaipur', 'Shaheed Smarak and route towards the BJP state headquarters, Jaipur', '2026-05-21', '2026-05-21', 'concluded', 'Congress workers marched in Jaipur on 21 May 2026 over alleged irregularities in NEET-UG. Police stopped the march at barricades, used water cannons and detained participants. The protest and police response are independently documented; injury reports and claims about the examination leak remain attributed.', 'occurrence_verified_disputed_details', '2026-07-17', '2026-07-17', 'candidate', 'in_national_pilot', '2026-05-21', 'Party claims concerning injuries and examination culpability require medical, police and investigative records. The protest is recorded separately from student-led protests.', 'one_day', 'Education', 'Accountability / resignation', 'NEET-UG examination accountability', '2026-05-21', '2026-06-21', 'Regional / local media', 'Nationally covered', 'Police used water cannons, detained participants and prevented the march from reaching the BJP headquarters.'),
  ('IO-CM-DL-0004', 'Delhi-NCR taxi, auto and transport unions hold three-day strike', 'Strike', 'Fuel prices, stagnant fares, app-aggregator commissions and transport operating costs', 'Delhi', 'Delhi-NCR', 'Delhi and adjoining NCR districts, including border protest points', '2026-05-21', '2026-05-23', 'concluded', 'Taxi, auto-rickshaw and commercial transport unions in Delhi-NCR began a three-day strike on 21 May 2026 over rising fuel costs, unchanged fares and other operating expenses. Participation and disruption varied across services. The strike and union demands are independently documented.', 'occurrence_verified_disputed_details', '2026-07-17', '2026-07-17', 'candidate', 'in_national_pilot', '2026-05-23', 'Reports described the first-day response as uneven. Claims about the number of unions, vehicles off road and commuter impact remain organiser or media estimates.', 'continuous', 'Labour & employment', 'Pay / operating-cost relief', 'Delhi-NCR fare regulation, fuel pricing and aggregator policy', null, '2026-06-15', 'National media search', 'Nationally covered', 'No comprehensive fare settlement was located during the three-day action.');

insert into public.claims (
  id, event_id, claim_text, claim_category, claimant, status, verification_notes,
  disputed_by, public_wording, publication_readiness
) values
  ('IO-CLM-MP-0001', 'IO-CM-MP-0001', 'A protest involving project-affected communities resumed in early July 2026.', 'Occurrence', 'India Observed synthesis', 'corroborated', 'Supported by Peek TV, Down To Earth and The Times of India. Peek TV cross-posts count as one underlying source.', null, 'Project-affected communities resumed a protest in early July 2026.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-MP-0002', 'IO-CM-MP-0001', 'The current phase of the protest began around 4 July 2026.', 'Start date / duration', 'India Observed synthesis', 'corroborated', 'Down To Earth published the resumption on 4 July; The Times of India described the protest as entering its sixth day on 9 July.', null, 'The current phase began around 4 July 2026.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-MP-0003', 'IO-CM-MP-0001', 'Reported protest forms include Chita Andolan, Jal Satyagraha, hunger strike and Mitti Satyagraha.', 'Protest method', 'Participants / media reports', 'corroborated', 'The forms are described across Down To Earth and The Times of India reporting.', null, 'Reported forms of protest include a symbolic Chita Andolan, Jal Satyagraha, hunger strike and Mitti Satyagraha.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-MP-0004', 'IO-CM-MP-0001', 'Participants are demanding compensation, rehabilitation and resettlement support.', 'Demand', 'Project-affected participants and organisers', 'corroborated', 'Consistently reported by Peek TV, Down To Earth and The Times of India.', null, 'Participants have publicly demanded compensation, rehabilitation and resettlement support.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-MP-0005', 'IO-CM-MP-0001', 'The protest concerns the Ken–Betwa Link Project and people affected by other development and irrigation projects.', 'Project connection', 'Participants / media reports', 'corroborated', 'Down To Earth and The Times of India identify Ken–Betwa as the principal project and mention additional projects.', null, 'The movement primarily concerns the Ken–Betwa Link Project and also includes people affected by other projects.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-MP-0006', 'IO-CM-MP-0001', 'Residents allege that homes were demolished during the monsoon before adequate rehabilitation was completed.', 'Displacement / demolition', 'Affected residents and movement representatives', 'attributed_allegation', 'Down To Earth provides field reporting and photographs, but legal responsibility, notice and adequacy of rehabilitation require official records and response.', 'District and project authorities', 'Affected residents allege that some homes were demolished during the monsoon before adequate rehabilitation was completed.', 'Ready with attribution'),
  ('IO-CLM-MP-0007', 'IO-CM-MP-0001', 'Protesters allege that drinking-water access at the protest site was stopped and that some participants became ill.', 'Public-service allegation', 'Protest participants / organisers', 'unconfirmed_allegation', 'Reported by The Times of India; no independent official or second-source confirmation has been located.', 'Chhatarpur district administration', 'Protesters alleged that drinking-water access at the site was interrupted; India Observed has not independently confirmed this.', 'Needs corroboration'),
  ('IO-CLM-MP-0008', 'IO-CM-MP-0001', 'The Chhatarpur district collector stated that no demands remained pending and that the protesters were from Panna district.', 'Official response', 'Chhatarpur district collector, as reported by The Times of India', 'attributed_official_statement', 'The statement is attributed through media reporting; obtain a direct district statement if available.', 'Protest participants / organisers', 'The Chhatarpur district collector told The Times of India that no demands remained pending and that the protesters were from Panna district.', 'Ready with attribution'),
  ('IO-CLM-MP-0009', 'IO-CM-MP-0001', 'An additional rehabilitation package of ₹202.5 crore was approved.', 'Compensation / package', 'Madhya Pradesh government, as reported by The Times of India', 'media_reported_official_document_required', 'The figure is reported by media. A cabinet decision, notification or project document should be added before presenting it as independently verified.', null, 'The Times of India reported that the state government had approved an additional ₹202.5 crore rehabilitation package.', 'Needs official document'),
  ('IO-CLM-MP-0010', 'IO-CM-MP-0001', 'Eligible families may receive a one-time rehabilitation grant of up to ₹12.5 lakh.', 'Compensation / package', 'Government representatives, as reported by The Times of India', 'media_reported_official_document_required', 'The eligibility criteria and amount require a direct government order or notification.', null, 'Media reports state that eligible families may receive a one-time rehabilitation grant of up to ₹12.5 lakh; the official eligibility document is still required.', 'Needs official document'),
  ('IO-CLM-MP-0011', 'IO-CM-MP-0001', 'The Ken–Betwa Link Project is officially intended to transfer water from the Ken basin to water-short areas of the Betwa basin and support irrigation and water supply.', 'Project context', 'National Water Development Agency', 'official_source_context', 'Supported by the official NWDA project page; this verifies project context, not the protesters'' allegations.', null, 'According to the National Water Development Agency, the project is intended to transfer water from the Ken basin to water-short areas of the Betwa basin and support irrigation and water supply.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-DL-0001', 'IO-CM-DL-0001', 'A CJP-led sit-in was continuing at Jantar Mantar in New Delhi in July 2026.', 'Occurrence', 'India Observed synthesis', 'corroborated', 'Supported by on-location Reuters reporting and independent NDTV and Hindustan Times coverage.', null, 'A CJP-led sit-in was continuing at Jantar Mantar in New Delhi in July 2026.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-DL-0002', 'IO-CM-DL-0001', 'The current sit-in began around 20 June 2026.', 'Start date / duration', 'India Observed synthesis', 'corroborated', 'Hindustan Times documented the second protest beginning on 20 June; later reporting described the protest as continuing for about 25 days by 15 July.', null, 'The current sit-in began around 20 June 2026.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-DL-0003', 'IO-CM-DL-0001', 'Sonam Wangchuk joined the protest through an indefinite hunger strike from 28 June 2026.', 'Protest method', 'Sonam Wangchuk / protest organisers', 'corroborated', 'Reuters, NDTV and Hindustan Times consistently report the start and duration of the fast.', null, 'Sonam Wangchuk joined the protest through an indefinite hunger strike from 28 June 2026.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-DL-0004', 'IO-CM-DL-0001', 'The immediate stated demand is the resignation of Union Education Minister Dharmendra Pradhan over alleged examination paper leaks and irregularities.', 'Demand', 'Cockroach Janta Party and supporting protesters', 'corroborated', 'The demand is consistently described by Reuters, NDTV and Hindustan Times. The underlying allegations remain subject to separate official and legal processes.', null, 'Protest organisers are demanding the resignation of Union Education Minister Dharmendra Pradhan over alleged examination paper leaks and irregularities.', 'Ready with attribution'),
  ('IO-CLM-DL-0005', 'IO-CM-DL-0001', 'Organisers reported that Wangchuk lost more than eight kilograms and experienced low blood sugar, weakness and muscle loss.', 'Other', 'Protest organisers / reported health bulletin', 'attributed_allegation', 'Reuters and NDTV report the organisers'' health bulletin; India Observed has not reviewed independent clinical records.', null, 'Organisers reported substantial weight loss and worsening weakness during the hunger strike; India Observed has not independently verified the medical measurements.', 'Ready with attribution'),
  ('IO-CLM-DL-0006', 'IO-CM-DL-0001', 'Dharmendra Pradhan rejected calls to resign and criticised the protest movement in an NDTV interview.', 'Official response', 'Dharmendra Pradhan, as reported by NDTV', 'attributed_official_statement', 'NDTV directly reports his response. Preserve attribution and avoid paraphrasing it as a general government position.', null, 'In an NDTV interview, Dharmendra Pradhan rejected calls to resign and criticised the protest movement.', 'Ready with attribution'),
  ('IO-CLM-DL-0007', 'IO-CM-DL-0001', 'Organisers announced a proposed march toward Parliament for 20 July 2026.', 'Outcome', 'Protest organisers', 'attributed_allegation', 'Reuters and other reports record the announcement. As of the review date, the proposed march had not yet occurred.', null, 'Organisers announced a proposed march for 20 July 2026; this is a future action, not a completed event.', 'Ready with attribution'),
  ('IO-CLM-KA-0001', 'IO-CM-KA-0001', 'Farmers protested in Mandya on 13 July 2026 over the delay in releasing irrigation water from KRS.', 'Occurrence', 'India Observed synthesis', 'corroborated', 'Supported by independent reporting from The Times of India and The New Indian Express.', null, 'Farmers protested in Mandya on 13 July 2026 over the delay in releasing irrigation water from KRS.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-KA-0002', 'IO-CM-KA-0001', 'The protesters demanded the immediate release of water into irrigation canals to protect standing crops.', 'Demand', 'Farmer organisations and participants', 'corroborated', 'Both independent reports identify this as the principal demand.', null, 'The protesters demanded the immediate release of water into irrigation canals to protect standing crops.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-KA-0003', 'IO-CM-KA-0001', 'Protesters said standing crops, particularly sugarcane, were drying because of the delay.', 'Other', 'Farmer organisations and participants', 'attributed_allegation', 'Reported by both outlets as the protesters'' assessment; no independent crop-loss measurement was reviewed.', null, 'Protesters said standing crops, particularly sugarcane, were drying because of the delay.', 'Ready with attribution'),
  ('IO-CLM-KA-0004', 'IO-CM-KA-0001', 'Protest actions included gathering near the deputy commissioner’s office and blocking the old Mysuru–Bengaluru highway at Sanjay Circle.', 'Protest method', 'India Observed synthesis', 'corroborated', 'The Times of India documents the deputy commissioner''s office protest; The New Indian Express reports the highway blockade and attempted siege.', null, 'Protest actions included gathering near the deputy commissioner’s office and blocking the old Mysuru–Bengaluru highway at Sanjay Circle.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-KA-0005', 'IO-CM-KA-0001', 'Protesters opposed additional Cauvery water use for a proposed drinking-water project while irrigation demands remained unmet.', 'Demand', 'Farmer organisations and participants', 'corroborated', 'The Times of India and The New Indian Express report opposition to the proposed additional drinking-water diversion.', null, 'Protesters opposed additional Cauvery water use for a proposed drinking-water project while irrigation demands remained unmet.', 'Ready with attribution'),
  ('IO-CLM-KA-0006', 'IO-CM-KA-0001', 'Farmer leaders warned that the agitation would intensify if the government did not respond.', 'Outcome', 'Farmer leaders', 'attributed_allegation', 'Reported as an organiser warning, not a completed escalation.', null, 'Farmer leaders warned that the agitation would intensify if the government did not respond.', 'Ready with attribution'),
  ('IO-CLM-CH-0001', 'IO-CM-CH-0001', 'BKU-Rajewal held a motorcycle and vehicle rally from Mohali to Chandigarh on 13 July 2026.', 'Occurrence', 'India Observed synthesis', 'corroborated', 'The Tribune and The Times of India independently document the date, route and gathering.', null, 'BKU-Rajewal held a motorcycle and vehicle rally from Mohali to Chandigarh on 13 July 2026.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-CH-0002', 'IO-CM-CH-0001', 'The rally travelled from Phase 8 in Mohali to the Exhibition Ground in Sector 34, Chandigarh.', 'Protest method', 'India Observed synthesis', 'corroborated', 'Both independent reports describe the route and destination.', null, 'The rally travelled from Phase 8 in Mohali to the Exhibition Ground in Sector 34, Chandigarh.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-CH-0003', 'IO-CM-CH-0001', 'The principal demand was that the proposed India–US trade agreement be rejected or cancelled.', 'Demand', 'Bharatiya Kisan Union (Rajewal)', 'corroborated', 'The demand is directly reported by The Tribune and The Times of India.', null, 'The organisers called for the proposed India–US trade agreement to be rejected.', 'Ready with attribution'),
  ('IO-CLM-CH-0004', 'IO-CM-CH-0001', 'Organisers argued that agricultural imports under the proposed agreement could disadvantage small farmers and allied sectors such as dairy and poultry.', 'Other', 'Bharatiya Kisan Union (Rajewal)', 'attributed_allegation', 'This is an economic prediction made by organisers; India Observed does not independently model the agreement''s effect.', null, 'Organisers argued that agricultural imports under the proposed agreement could disadvantage small farmers and allied sectors.', 'Ready with attribution'),
  ('IO-CLM-CH-0005', 'IO-CM-CH-0001', 'Organisers also raised concerns about groundwater quality, land acquisition, climate pressures and natural resources in Punjab.', 'Demand', 'Bharatiya Kisan Union (Rajewal)', 'corroborated', 'The concerns are reported across the two independent reports.', null, 'Organisers also raised Punjab-specific concerns about groundwater quality, land acquisition, climate pressures and natural resources.', 'Ready with attribution'),
  ('IO-CLM-CH-0006', 'IO-CM-CH-0001', 'BKU leaders submitted memorandums addressed to the Prime Minister through the Punjab governor and to the Punjab chief minister.', 'Outcome', 'Bharatiya Kisan Union (Rajewal)', 'corroborated', 'The Times of India reports the two memorandums; The Tribune documents the rally and demands.', null, 'BKU leaders submitted memorandums addressed to the Prime Minister through the Punjab governor and to the Punjab chief minister.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-CH-0007', 'IO-CM-CH-0001', 'Traffic restrictions and diversions were imposed and congestion was reported along the route.', 'Official response', 'Chandigarh Police / media reports', 'corroborated', 'Both outlets report police restrictions and substantial traffic disruption.', null, 'Chandigarh Police imposed temporary restrictions and diversions, and congestion was reported along the rally route.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-MH-0001', 'IO-CM-MH-0001', 'A Save SGNP protest and human chain took place in Thane on Sunday, 5 July 2026.', 'Occurrence', 'India Observed synthesis', 'corroborated', 'The Times of India reports the Sunday gathering on 5 July. Free Press Journal independently describes the same protest but gives an inconsistent calendar date.', null, 'A Save SGNP protest and human chain took place in Thane on Sunday, 5 July 2026.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-MH-0002', 'IO-CM-MH-0001', 'Participants gathered near the Chitalsar Manpada entry point and formed a human chain along part of the Tikuji-ni-Wadi–Khewra Chowk stretch.', 'Protest method', 'India Observed synthesis', 'corroborated', 'The gathering point is reported by The Times of India; the human-chain stretch is described by Free Press Journal.', null, 'Participants gathered near the Chitalsar Manpada entry point and formed a human chain along part of the Tikuji-ni-Wadi–Khewra Chowk stretch.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-MH-0003', 'IO-CM-MH-0001', 'The campaign opposed infrastructure and construction proposals that participants believed could damage forests near SGNP.', 'Demand', 'Mission Save SGNP participants', 'corroborated', 'Both independent reports describe opposition to development proposals around the park.', null, 'The campaign opposed infrastructure and construction proposals that participants said could damage forests near SGNP.', 'Ready with attribution'),
  ('IO-CLM-MH-0004', 'IO-CM-MH-0001', 'One stated demand was to halt a Thane Municipal Corporation proposal for a man-made biodiversity park in an area protesters described as an existing natural ecosystem.', 'Demand', 'Mission Save SGNP participants', 'attributed_allegation', 'The Times of India reports the demand. Official project documents and land boundaries have not yet been added.', null, 'One stated demand was to halt a proposed man-made biodiversity park in an area protesters described as an existing natural ecosystem.', 'Ready with attribution'),
  ('IO-CLM-MH-0005', 'IO-CM-MH-0001', 'Campaign material seeks protection of approximately 193 acres of forest land near the park.', 'Project context', 'Mission Save SGNP campaign', 'attributed_allegation', 'The figure appears in the public campaign petition and campaign posts; official cadastral or forest records are required.', null, 'Campaign material seeks protection of approximately 193 acres of forest land near the park; official land records are still required.', 'Needs official document'),
  ('IO-CLM-MH-0006', 'IO-CM-MH-0001', 'The protest continued despite heavy rain.', 'Other', 'India Observed synthesis', 'corroborated', 'Both independent reports mention heavy rainfall during the gathering.', null, 'The protest continued despite heavy rain.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-MH-0007', 'IO-CM-MH-0001', 'Campaign posts stated that more than 1,000 people participated.', 'Other', 'Mission Save SGNP campaign posts', 'unconfirmed_allegation', 'Media described hundreds or a large gathering, while campaign posts claimed over 1,000. India Observed has not independently counted participants.', null, 'Campaign posts stated that more than 1,000 people participated; India Observed has not independently verified the attendance figure.', 'Needs corroboration'),
  ('IO-CLM-KA-0007', 'IO-CM-KA-0002', 'Farmers and agricultural communities in the Bidadi region have conducted a sustained movement opposing the township land acquisition.', 'Occurrence', 'India Observed synthesis', 'corroborated', 'Supported by independent reporting from The News Minute, The New Indian Express and The Times of India.', null, 'Farmers and agricultural communities in the Bidadi region have conducted a sustained movement opposing the township land acquisition.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-KA-0008', 'IO-CM-KA-0002', 'By 29 June 2026, farmers had been protesting for more than 450 days.', 'Start date / duration', 'The News Minute ground report', 'corroborated', 'The News Minute''s ground report and July survey coverage independently describe a movement lasting more than 450 days. The exact first day remains under verification.', null, 'Independent reporting described the movement as having continued for more than 450 days by late June 2026.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-KA-0009', 'IO-CM-KA-0002', 'The Karnataka government issued a final notification in June 2026 for first-phase acquisition of approximately 518 acres across Kempayyanapalya, Mandalahalli and Vaderahalli.', 'Project connection', 'Karnataka Government, as documented by independent media', 'corroborated', 'The News Minute and The New Indian Express independently report the final notification and the three villages. A direct gazette copy has not yet been added.', null, 'Independent reports state that the Karnataka government issued a final notification in June 2026 for approximately 518 acres across three villages in the first phase.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-KA-0010', 'IO-CM-KA-0002', 'The movement''s principal demand is that the government stop, withdraw or reconsider the land acquisition and protect affected farming livelihoods.', 'Demand', 'Raithara Bhoohitha Rakshana Sangha and affected farmers', 'corroborated', 'This demand is consistently described in ground reports, the Appiko protest report and survey-resistance coverage.', null, 'Protesters are demanding that the government stop, withdraw or reconsider the land acquisition and protect affected farming livelihoods.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-KA-0011', 'IO-CM-KA-0002', 'Farmers organised under the banner of the Raithara Bhoohitha Rakshana Sangha.', 'Other', 'The News Minute ground report', 'corroborated', 'The organisation is named in The News Minute''s ground reporting. Its formal registration and office-bearer details still require confirmation.', null, 'Farmers have organised under the banner of the Raithara Bhoohitha Rakshana Sangha.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-KA-0012', 'IO-CM-KA-0002', 'The government describes the township as a project intended to decongest Bengaluru, support economic growth and create employment.', 'Official response', 'Karnataka Government, as reported by The News Minute and The New Indian Express', 'attributed_official_statement', 'The stated objectives are reported consistently, but a complete official project plan has not yet been added.', null, 'The Karnataka government describes the township as a planned urban-development and employment project intended to support Bengaluru''s growth.', 'Ready with attribution'),
  ('IO-CLM-KA-0013', 'IO-CM-KA-0002', 'The government has proposed cash compensation in the range of approximately ₹2.07 crore to ₹2.14 crore per acre and other compensation options.', 'Compensation / package', 'Karnataka Government, as reported by The News Minute', 'media_reported_official_document_required', 'The News Minute reports the compensation range and applications. The underlying compensation order and eligibility terms are still required.', null, 'Media reports state that the government proposed cash compensation of approximately ₹2.07 crore to ₹2.14 crore per acre; the official compensation order is still required.', 'Needs official document'),
  ('IO-CLM-KA-0014', 'IO-CM-KA-0002', 'Farmers staged an Appiko tree-hugging protest on 28 June 2026 to oppose the project and raise concerns about loss of green cover.', 'Protest method', 'Affected farmers', 'corroborated', 'The Times of India documented the march and tree-hugging action with location and participant details.', null, 'Farmers staged an Appiko tree-hugging protest on 28 June 2026 to oppose the project and raise environmental concerns.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-KA-0015', 'IO-CM-KA-0002', 'On 13 July 2026, farmers stopped or obstructed a government land-survey team in Mandalahalli and a confrontation occurred.', 'Protest method', 'India Observed synthesis', 'corroborated', 'The News Minute, India Today and The New Indian Express independently document the survey obstruction and confrontation. Responsibility for injuries, stone throwing and vehicle damage is disputed.', null, 'On 13 July 2026, protesters stopped or obstructed a government land-survey team in Mandalahalli and a confrontation occurred.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-KA-0016', 'IO-CM-KA-0002', 'Police registered two FIRs following the 13 July confrontation, alleging assault, obstruction and damage by protesters.', 'Official response', 'Karnataka Police, as reported by India Today and The New Indian Express', 'attributed_official_statement', 'The allegations come from FIRs and police complaints. A farmer quoted by India Today denied that members of the farmers'' association were responsible for the alleged violence.', 'Protesting farmers / association members', 'Police registered two FIRs following the confrontation, alleging assault, obstruction and damage; representatives of the movement disputed responsibility for the violence.', 'Ready with attribution'),
  ('IO-CLM-KA-0017', 'IO-CM-KA-0002', 'Farmers say the acquisition threatens productive agricultural land, farming livelihoods and local green cover.', 'Other', 'Affected farmers and farmer organisations', 'attributed_allegation', 'Ground reporting documents active cultivation and farmer testimony. Exact land-use classification, agricultural productivity and environmental loss require official land, horticulture and environmental records.', null, 'Farmers say the acquisition threatens agricultural livelihoods, productive land and local green cover; the exact scale remains under review.', 'Ready with attribution'),
  ('IO-CLM-KA-0018', 'IO-CM-KA-0002', 'Claims about the proportion of landowners who consented to acquisition are disputed.', 'Other', 'Government representatives and protesting farmers', 'disputed', 'Government and protest participants have presented conflicting accounts about farmer acceptance and compensation applications. No complete consent register has been reviewed.', null, 'Government representatives and protesting farmers have presented conflicting accounts about consent and participation in the compensation process.', 'Ready with attribution'),
  ('IO-CLM-KA-0019', 'IO-CM-KA-0002', 'On 15 July 2026, the Karnataka government announced a committee to review the proposed township amid the continuing protests.', 'Official response', 'Karnataka Government, as reported by The Economic Times', 'media_reported_official_document_required', 'The announcement is reported by The Economic Times. A direct government notification naming the committee, members and mandate has not yet been located.', null, 'The Economic Times reported that the Karnataka government announced a committee to review the proposed township amid the protests.', 'Needs official document'),
  ('IO-CLM-GJ-0001', 'IO-CM-GJ-0001', 'Farmers centred in Jetpar village began a protest on 7 June 2026 over compensation for agricultural land affected by transmission infrastructure.', 'Occurrence', 'India Observed synthesis', 'corroborated', 'Independent reports from The Indian Express, The Wire and The Telegraph document the movement and its chronology.', null, 'Farmers centred in Jetpar village began a protest on 7 June 2026 over compensation for land affected by transmission infrastructure.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-GJ-0002', 'IO-CM-GJ-0001', 'A group of farmers began an indefinite hunger strike on 17 June 2026.', 'Protest method', 'Affected farmers', 'corroborated', 'The start of the hunger strike is consistently reported by multiple independent publishers.', null, 'A group of farmers began an indefinite hunger strike on 17 June 2026.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-GJ-0003', 'IO-CM-GJ-0001', 'Farmers demanded compensation based on four times the market value and changes to right-of-way compensation.', 'Demand', 'Affected farmers and farmer organisations', 'corroborated', 'The demand is consistently described across the independent reporting; the legal entitlement remains a policy and valuation question.', null, 'Farmers demanded compensation based on four times the market value and changes to right-of-way compensation.', 'Ready with attribution'),
  ('IO-CLM-GJ-0004', 'IO-CM-GJ-0001', 'The transmission project is being implemented through Halvad Transmission Limited, associated with Adani Energy Solutions.', 'Project connection', 'Media reports and company/project references', 'corroborated', 'The implementing entity is identified by multiple reports. The complete concession and route documents have not yet been added.', null, 'Independent reports identify Halvad Transmission Limited, associated with Adani Energy Solutions, as the project implementing entity.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-GJ-0005', 'IO-CM-GJ-0001', 'On 4 July 2026, the Gujarat government issued revised compensation guidelines that included a higher land-valuation basis and a new valuation process.', 'Official response', 'Gujarat Government, as reported by independent media', 'media_reported_official_document_required', 'The revised resolution is described by The Indian Express, The Wire and The Telegraph. The original government resolution must still be added.', null, 'Independent reports state that the Gujarat government issued revised compensation guidelines on 4 July 2026; the original resolution is still required.', 'Needs official document'),
  ('IO-CLM-GJ-0006', 'IO-CM-GJ-0001', 'Farmers ended the hunger strike on 7 July but said the wider protest would continue as a satyagraha.', 'Outcome', 'Affected farmers and organisers', 'corroborated', 'The change in protest form is independently reported after the government announcement.', null, 'Farmers ended the hunger strike on 7 July but said the wider protest would continue as a satyagraha.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-GJ-0007', 'IO-CM-GJ-0001', 'Farmers allege that tower foundations and transmission corridors can make portions of their agricultural land difficult or impossible to cultivate.', 'Other', 'Affected farmers', 'attributed_allegation', 'The impact is described through farmer testimony. Parcel-level agricultural and engineering assessments have not been reviewed.', null, 'Farmers say tower foundations and transmission corridors reduce the cultivable use of affected land; the exact impact remains under review.', 'Ready with attribution'),
  ('IO-CLM-GJ-0008', 'IO-CM-GJ-0001', 'Sources provide differing technical figures for the project''s voltage and route length.', 'Project context', 'Independent media reports', 'disputed', 'Published reports use differing figures, including 756 kV versus 765 kV and different route-length descriptions. Official project documents are required.', null, 'Published reports provide differing technical descriptions of the transmission project; India Observed has not selected one figure pending official documents.', 'Needs official document'),
  ('IO-CLM-UP-0001', 'IO-CM-UP-0001', 'Residents of Dasiya and nearby villages were publicly opposing the proposed ethanol plant by at least 23 June 2026.', 'Occurrence', 'India Observed synthesis', 'corroborated', 'Amar Ujala documented a memorandum and public opposition in June; later local reporting documented the July demonstration.', null, 'Residents of Dasiya and nearby villages were publicly opposing the proposed ethanol plant by at least 23 June 2026.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-UP-0002', 'IO-CM-UP-0001', 'A larger demonstration against the plant took place on 14 July 2026 under substantial police deployment.', 'Occurrence', 'India Observed synthesis', 'corroborated', 'The event is documented by Navbharat Times and public field video from the site.', null, 'A larger demonstration against the plant took place on 14 July 2026 under substantial police deployment.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-UP-0003', 'IO-CM-UP-0001', 'The principal demand was that construction or operation of the ethanol plant be stopped.', 'Demand', 'Residents and supporting local organisations', 'corroborated', 'The demand appears consistently in the memorandum reporting, demonstration coverage and field material.', null, 'Residents and supporting organisations called for the ethanol-plant project to be stopped.', 'Ready with attribution'),
  ('IO-CLM-UP-0004', 'IO-CM-UP-0001', 'Protesters raised concerns about groundwater use, pollution, public health and effects on nearby settlements and schools.', 'Other', 'Residents and organisers', 'attributed_allegation', 'These concerns are consistently reported as the protesters'' stated reasons. No environmental-impact assessment or pollution-control consent has yet been added.', null, 'Protesters raised concerns about water use, pollution, health and effects on nearby settlements and schools.', 'Ready with attribution'),
  ('IO-CLM-UP-0005', 'IO-CM-UP-0001', 'Local reports state that approximately 14 to 15 villages and two government schools are located near the project area.', 'Project context', 'Residents and local media reports', 'media_reported_official_document_required', 'The figures require confirmation through maps, school records and project documents.', null, 'Local reports state that several villages and two government schools are near the project area; the exact number requires official verification.', 'Needs official document'),
  ('IO-CLM-UP-0006', 'IO-CM-UP-0001', 'Some residents allege that landholders were not initially told that an ethanol plant would be built.', 'Other', 'Affected residents', 'unconfirmed_allegation', 'The allegation appears in local reporting but has not been tested against sale deeds, consent records or project-disclosure documents.', null, 'Some residents allege that landholders were not initially told that the project would be an ethanol plant; India Observed has not independently confirmed this.', 'Needs official document'),
  ('IO-CLM-UP-0007', 'IO-CM-UP-0001', 'Police and district authorities restricted access near the factory site and prevented some political representatives from reaching the demonstration.', 'Official response', 'Police and district authorities, as documented by media', 'corroborated', 'Navbharat Times and field reporting document heavy deployment and restrictions. The legal basis and exact orders have not been added.', null, 'Police and district authorities restricted access near the factory site and prevented some political representatives from reaching the demonstration.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-UP-0008', 'IO-CM-UP-0001', 'Media reports describe the proposed investment as approximately ₹500 crore.', 'Project context', 'Local media reports', 'media_reported_official_document_required', 'The amount is reported in media but requires a company filing, industrial approval or government investment document.', null, 'Media reports describe the proposed investment as approximately ₹500 crore; an official project document is still required.', 'Needs official document'),
  ('IO-CLM-AS-0001', 'IO-CM-AS-0001', 'Hundreds of Bodo residents gathered at Malgaon on 12 July 2026 to protest a proposed land allotment and resettlement plan.', 'Occurrence', 'India Observed synthesis', 'corroborated', 'India Today North East video reporting and local community coverage document the gathering and its purpose.', null, 'Hundreds of Bodo residents gathered at Malgaon on 12 July 2026 to protest a proposed land allotment and resettlement plan.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-AS-0002', 'IO-CM-AS-0001', 'The protesters opposed proposed allotment of land to Assam Power Distribution Company Limited.', 'Demand', 'Greater Malgaon residents', 'corroborated', 'The demand is consistently described in regional and community reporting.', null, 'Protesters opposed the proposed allotment of land to Assam Power Distribution Company Limited.', 'Ready with attribution'),
  ('IO-CLM-AS-0003', 'IO-CM-AS-0001', 'The protesters also opposed a proposal to rehabilitate 93 families evicted from Kaimari on the same or nearby land.', 'Demand', 'Greater Malgaon residents', 'corroborated', 'The number and proposal are consistently reported, but the formal rehabilitation order has not been located.', null, 'Protesters also opposed a proposal to rehabilitate 93 families evicted from Kaimari on the land in question.', 'Ready with attribution'),
  ('IO-CLM-AS-0004', 'IO-CM-AS-0001', 'Protesters demanded withdrawal of the proposals and protection of land they described as part of a Tribal Belt and Block.', 'Demand', 'Greater Malgaon residents', 'corroborated', 'This is the central stated demand across the reviewed sources.', null, 'Protesters demanded withdrawal of the proposals and protection of land they described as part of a Tribal Belt and Block.', 'Ready with attribution'),
  ('IO-CLM-AS-0005', 'IO-CM-AS-0001', 'Community representatives said the land had protected Tribal Belt and Block status since 1984.', 'Project context', 'Community representatives', 'media_reported_official_document_required', 'The legal status and date require revenue notifications, cadastral records or other official land documents.', null, 'Community representatives said the land has had protected Tribal Belt and Block status since 1984; official land records are still required.', 'Needs official document'),
  ('IO-CLM-AS-0006', 'IO-CM-AS-0001', 'Protesters alleged that the proposals were made without adequate consultation and would weaken legal protections for tribal land.', 'Other', 'Community representatives', 'attributed_allegation', 'The consultation process and legal effect require government files and land-law analysis.', null, 'Protesters alleged that the proposals were made without adequate consultation and would weaken protections for tribal land.', 'Ready with attribution'),
  ('IO-CLM-AS-0007', 'IO-CM-AS-0001', 'No direct response from the Assam government, Bodoland Territorial Council or APDCL had been located by the review date.', 'Official response', 'India Observed review', 'unconfirmed_allegation', 'This records the limits of the reviewed source set, not proof that no response exists.', null, 'India Observed had not located a direct government, BTC or APDCL response by 15 July 2026.', 'Ready with attribution'),
  ('IO-CLM-MN-0001', 'IO-CM-MN-0001', 'The Manipur Government Services Federation launched an indefinite cease-work strike on 1 July 2026.', 'Occurrence', 'India Observed synthesis', 'corroborated', 'The launch date and federation are consistently reported by The Sangai Express and later regional reporting.', null, 'The Manipur Government Services Federation launched an indefinite cease-work strike on 1 July 2026.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-MN-0002', 'IO-CM-MN-0001', 'The strike continued through at least 15 July 2026.', 'Start date / duration', 'India Observed synthesis', 'corroborated', 'Regional reporting documents the strike''s ninth day and subsequent continuation after a partial government response.', null, 'The strike continued through at least 15 July 2026.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-MN-0003', 'IO-CM-MN-0001', 'The federation''s demands included dearness-allowance parity, restoration of the old pension scheme, a higher retirement age, regularisation of contractual employees and restoration of Saturday holidays.', 'Demand', 'Manipur Government Services Federation', 'corroborated', 'The principal charter is reported consistently across launch and follow-up coverage.', null, 'The federation''s demands included dearness-allowance parity, pension changes, retirement-age revision, regularisation and restoration of Saturday holidays.', 'Ready with attribution'),
  ('IO-CLM-MN-0004', 'IO-CM-MN-0001', 'The cease-work action significantly disrupted routine work in government offices.', 'Other', 'Independent regional media reports', 'corroborated', 'Multiple reports describe widespread administrative disruption; exact office-by-office participation is not available.', null, 'The cease-work action significantly disrupted routine work in government offices.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-MN-0005', 'IO-CM-MN-0001', 'The Manipur government restored Saturday as a holiday and introduced a five-day working week for government offices.', 'Official response', 'Manipur Government', 'corroborated', 'The decision is consistently reported as a government response and was followed by continuation of the strike.', null, 'The Manipur government restored Saturday as a holiday and introduced a five-day working week for government offices.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-MN-0006', 'IO-CM-MN-0001', 'The federation said the strike would continue because its other demands remained unresolved.', 'Outcome', 'Manipur Government Services Federation', 'corroborated', 'Regional reporting documents continuation after the Saturday-holiday decision.', null, 'The federation said the strike would continue because its other demands remained unresolved.', 'Ready with attribution'),
  ('IO-CLM-MN-0007', 'IO-CM-MN-0001', 'A reported estimate placed the state''s financial loss during the first nine days at ₹13.28 crore.', 'Other', 'Reported administrative estimate', 'media_reported_official_document_required', 'The figure is carried by media and should not be treated as an independently audited loss.', null, 'Media reports cited an estimated loss of ₹13.28 crore during the first nine days; India Observed has not independently audited the figure.', 'Needs official document'),
  ('IO-CLM-MN-0008', 'IO-CM-MN-0001', 'The MGSF strike is distinct from separate July cease-work actions organised by other employee federations or joint committees.', 'Project context', 'India Observed editorial distinction', 'corroborated', 'Reviewed reports name different organising bodies and demand charters. They should not be merged without evidence of coordination.', null, 'The MGSF-led strike is recorded separately from other employee cease-work actions unless coordination is independently confirmed.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-OD-0001', 'IO-CM-OD-0001', 'Students locked the gate of Dharmasala Baneepeetha High School and staged a dharna on 10 July 2026.', 'Occurrence', 'India Observed synthesis', 'corroborated', 'The New Indian Express and The Times of India independently report the date, location and action.', null, 'Students locked the school gate and staged a dharna on 10 July 2026.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-OD-0002', 'IO-CM-OD-0001', 'The students demanded immediate appointment or deputation of teachers to fill vacancies.', 'Demand', 'Students and guardians', 'corroborated', 'Both independent reports identify teacher vacancies as the central demand.', null, 'Students demanded immediate appointment or deputation of teachers to address vacancies.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-OD-0003', 'IO-CM-OD-0001', 'The school''s sanctioned teacher strength was reported as 16.', 'Project context', 'School and education-office records as reported by media', 'corroborated', 'Both reports use a sanctioned strength of 16 teachers.', null, 'Independent reports state that the school had a sanctioned strength of 16 teachers.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-OD-0004', 'IO-CM-OD-0001', 'Reports differed on whether 10 or 11 teachers were in position at the time of the protest.', 'Other', 'Independent media reports', 'disputed', 'The Times of India reported 10 teachers; The New Indian Express reported 11. The difference may reflect timing or counting method.', null, 'Independent reports differed on whether 10 or 11 teachers were in position; India Observed has not resolved the discrepancy.', 'Ready with attribution'),
  ('IO-CLM-OD-0005', 'IO-CM-OD-0001', 'Reports also differed on whether the school served more than 400 or 508 students and on the class levels counted.', 'Other', 'Independent media reports', 'disputed', 'The reports appear to count different class groupings. School enrolment records are needed.', null, 'Reports differed on the number of students and class levels counted; official enrolment data is still required.', 'Needs official document'),
  ('IO-CLM-OD-0006', 'IO-CM-OD-0001', 'District education officials deputed two teachers to the school on the day of the protest.', 'Official response', 'Jajpur District Education Office', 'corroborated', 'Both reports describe the immediate deputation of two teachers.', null, 'District education officials deputed two teachers to the school on the day of the protest.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-OD-0007', 'IO-CM-OD-0001', 'Students withdrew the dharna after the deputation of two teachers.', 'Outcome', 'Students and school authorities', 'corroborated', 'The withdrawal is reported by both independent outlets.', null, 'Students withdrew the dharna after two teachers were deputed.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-UK-0001', 'IO-CM-UK-0001', 'Residents and environmental activists publicly protested tree felling linked to the Bhaniyawala–Rishikesh road-widening project in July 2026.', 'Occurrence', 'India Observed synthesis', 'corroborated', 'Avikal Uttarakhand documented a protest at the NHAI office on 8 July; The Times of India independently documented continuing roadside protests by 11 July.', null, 'Residents and environmental activists publicly protested tree felling linked to the Bhaniyawala–Rishikesh road-widening project in July 2026.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-UK-0002', 'IO-CM-UK-0001', 'The movement included a demonstration at the NHAI office, tree-hugging actions and sit-ins along the road stretch.', 'Protest method', 'Residents and environmental activists', 'corroborated', 'The protest methods are described across independent local reporting and later follow-up coverage.', null, 'The movement included a demonstration at the NHAI office, tree-hugging actions and sit-ins along the road stretch.', 'Ready'),
  ('IO-CLM-UK-0003', 'IO-CM-UK-0001', 'The Times of India reported on 11 July 2026 that the protest had entered its fifth consecutive day.', 'Start date / duration', 'India Observed synthesis', 'corroborated', 'This suggests activity began around 7 July, but the Events register uses 8 July as the earliest directly reviewed dated protest.', null, 'On 11 July 2026, The Times of India reported that the protest had entered its fifth consecutive day.', 'Ready with attribution'),
  ('IO-CLM-UK-0004', 'IO-CM-UK-0001', 'Tree felling resumed under police deployment on 13 July, and media reported that two demonstrators were arrested and an FIR registered against around two dozen unidentified people.', 'Official response', 'Police and NHAI, as reported by The Times of India', 'corroborated', 'The report includes attributed police statements. The existence of arrests and an FIR is recorded; allegations within the FIR are not treated as proven.', null, 'The Times of India reported that tree felling resumed under police deployment and that two demonstrators were arrested, with an FIR registered against around two dozen unidentified people.', 'Ready with attribution'),
  ('IO-CLM-UK-0005', 'IO-CM-UK-0001', 'Protesters demanded that tree felling be halted or deferred and that the road-widening plan be reconsidered on environmental grounds.', 'Demand', 'Residents and environmental activists', 'corroborated', 'The central demand is consistent across Avikal Uttarakhand and The Times of India reporting.', null, 'Protesters demanded that tree felling be halted or deferred and that the road-widening plan be reconsidered on environmental grounds.', 'Ready with attribution'),
  ('IO-CLM-UK-0006', 'IO-CM-UK-0001', 'Reviewed sources use different figures for the number of trees proposed for felling or transplantation.', 'Other', 'India Observed review', 'disputed', 'Reviewed reporting uses figures including around 3,000, around 4,000 and 4,369 trees, while official material identifies 754 trees as suitable for transplantation. Direct project and forest-clearance documents are required before selecting a single total.', null, 'Reviewed sources use differing figures for the number of trees affected; India Observed has not selected a single total pending direct project and forest-clearance documents.', 'Needs official document'),
  ('IO-CLM-UK-0007', 'IO-CM-UK-0001', 'The Ministry of Road Transport and Highways described the project as approximately 20 kilometres long, estimated at ₹743 crore, with the right of way reduced from 60 metres to 23 metres and 754 trees identified as suitable for transplantation.', 'Project context', 'Ministry of Road Transport and Highways / Press Information Bureau', 'official_source_context', 'Supported by the official PIB project release. This verifies the government''s project description, not the protesters'' environmental-impact claims.', null, 'According to the Ministry of Road Transport and Highways, the project is approximately 20 kilometres long, is estimated at ₹743 crore, uses a reduced right of way and identifies 754 trees as suitable for transplantation.', 'Ready'),
